    <DataNode elementId="Sphingoids" textLabel="a sphingoid base" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="MNXM146258" dataSource="MetaNetX" />
      <Graphics centerX="350" centerY="400" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, zhang">Sphingoids (sphingoid bases, or long chain bases) are building blocks of |FRAME: SPHINGOLIPIDS sphingolipids|. They are amino alcohols, composed predominantly (but not exclusively) of 18 carbon atoms. They are characterized by the presence of a hydroxyl group at C1 (and often also at C3), and an amine group at C2. The commonly known sphingoids include |FRAME: SPHINGOSINE|, |FRAME: D-erythro-Shinganines sphinganine| (dihydrosphingosine), and |FRAME: Phytosphingosines phytosphingosine| (4-hydroxysphinganine).</Comment>
