    <DataNode elementId="VLC-Ceramides" textLabel="a very-long-chain ceramide" type="Metabolite">
      <Graphics centerX="350" centerY="500" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="SRI, caspi">A very-long-chain ceramide is a lipid molecule that is composed of |FRAME: Sphingoids| and |FRAME: Very-long-chain-fatty-acids|. Ceramides are found in high concentrations within the cell membrane and are one of the component lipids that make up |FRAME: Sphingomyelins sphingomyelin|, one of the major lipids in the lipid bilayer.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="VLC-Ceramides" />
